1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,310
Why does your tongue stick to a frozen

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:03,010
pole?

3
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:05,140
Because your own spit just turned into

4
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:05,840
glue.

5
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:08,280
Metal steals heat far faster than wood or

6
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:10,540
plastic. Touch it, and the warmth drains

7
00:00:10,540 --> 00:00:12,700
out of your wet tongue in a flash.

8
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,060
The spit freezes solid, into the tiny

9
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:16,820
bumps of your tongue and the tiny pits

10
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:17,520
in the metal.

11
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,620
Now ice locks them together.

12
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:21,860
Pull hard, and that ice can tear skin

13
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:22,940
right off.

14
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:24,040
So never pull.

15
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,580
Pour on warm water, the ice glue melts...

16
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:27,740
and you're free.
